69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: no, the crux is the line document.getElementById(&quot;foo&quot;).appendChild(document.createElement(&quot;span&quot;))
my confusion is with &quot;Firefox appends more text to the last text node it was appending to&quot;, since if a script is running, the last text node it inserted into was the &lt;script&gt;'s child node
you're saying you want     &lt;script&gt;write 'aaa'; append element node&lt;/script&gt;bbb  to result in &quot;aaabbb element node&quot; rather than &quot;aaa element node bbb&quot;?
